     1	//! Z-order (Morton) curve hashing used to speed up the ear test on larger
     2	//! polygons.
     3	//!
     4	//! `earcut.hpp` switches this on once the input exceeds 80 vertices, so both
     5	//! the plain and the hashed ear tests have to be bit-faithful.
